    "source_turn_preview_server_only": "Some roads use paving materials that allow rain to move through tiny openings. This approach, known as permeable paving, can reduce runoff where soil conditions permit. But it needs maintenance: fine material can clog the openings, and unsuitable ground may prevent proper infiltration. The installation is therefore not a universal replacement for drainage pipes."
